{
  "_comment": [
    "Shared fixtures for the Python-engine parity proof.",
    "tools/engine_parity.js runs each case through the shipped n8n code nodes and writes n8n/parity-golden.json;",
    "tools/engine_parity.py runs the same case through backend/engine.py and diffs the two traces.",
    "A case is: id, env (the $env the workflow would see), payload (the webhook body), headers (webhook",
    "headers, i.e. the BYOK route), responses (what the gateway returned per lane; a lane that is absent",
    "from the map is a lane whose branch never ran).",
    "Add a case whenever engine.py grows a branch, or whenever a workflow node changes and the golden is",
    "re-recorded. Cases with a harness_error mean the FIXTURE is wrong, not the port."
  ],
